# Generated files — Prettier must not rewrite these.
#
# `lint-staged` runs `prettier --write` over `*.{json,md}`, which would reformat
# a generated document on every commit that touches it. The generator would then
# undo that on its next run, so the file would flip between two formattings
# forever and every regeneration would carry thousands of lines of pure noise.
# The fix is to leave generated output exactly as its generator emits it.

# Rendered from Base.metadata by backend/scripts/generate_schema_docs.py
docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA.md

# Rendered from the training guides by scripts/screenshots/status_report.py
docs/training/SCREENSHOT_STATUS.md

# Files carrying multi-line SCREENSHOT NEEDED markers.
#
# The marker convention is `> **[SCREENSHOT NEEDED — …]**` opening a blockquote
# whose closing `**]**` sits several lines later. Prettier reads that opening
# `**` as unmatched emphasis and escapes it to `\*\*`, which does not change how
# the page reads — and silently removes the marker from
# `scripts/screenshots/status_report.py`, whose pattern anchors on `^>\s*\*\*\[?`.
#
# `lint-staged` runs `prettier --write` over `*.md`, so without this a commit
# touching one of these files can drop tracked screenshot requests with no
# visible diff in the rendered prose. That is the failure recorded in
# SCREENSHOT_CURRENCY.md under "0 remaining was measuring the wrong thing".
#
# The criterion is deliberately "carries a multi-line marker", not "Prettier
# breaks it today". Whether a given marker escapes depends on surrounding
# context, so a file that survives now can flip the next time one is added.
# Listing prose-formatting off a file costs nothing that matters; losing a
# tracked capture silently does. Re-derive the list with:
#
#   python3 - <<'EOF'
#   import glob, re
#   for f in sorted(glob.glob('docs/training/*.md')):
#       for L in open(f).read().split('\n'):
#           if re.match(r'^>\s*\*\*\[?\s*SCREENSHOT NEEDED', L, re.I) \
#              and not L.rstrip().endswith('**]**'):
#               print(f); break
#   EOF
#
# Take a file off the list once it has no multi-line markers left.
docs/training/03-scheduling.md
docs/training/04-events-meetings.md
docs/training/09-skills-testing.md
